Focusing on optimizing collision detection by reducing the number of collision checks and using spatial partitioning is a great approach. Here are specific steps you can take to implement these changes:

### Step 1: Reduce Collision Checks

#### 1.1. **Collision Filtering**
   - **Layer-Based Filtering:** Divide objects into different layers based on their types (e.g., vehicles, pedestrians, buildings). Configure the physics engine to only perform collision checks between relevant layers.
     ```cpp
     // Example in PhysX
     PxFilterFlags filterShader(
         PxFilterObjectAttributes attributes0, PxFilterData filterData0,
         PxFilterObjectAttributes attributes1, PxFilterData filterData1,
         PxPairFlags& pairFlags, bool& disablePreprocessing)
     {
         pairFlags = PxPairFlag::eCONTACT_DEFAULT;
         disablePreprocessing = false;

         // Define layers and their interactions
         const uint32_t layerMask0 = filterData0.word0;
         const uint32_t layerMask1 = filterData1.word0;

         // Example: Vehicles collide with pedestrians but not with buildings
         if ((layerMask0 & 0x01) && (layerMask1 & 0x02)) {
             return PxFilterFlag::eDEFAULT;
         }
         return PxFilterFlag::eNONE;
     }
     ```

#### 1.2. **Group Objects Efficiently**
   - **Group Similar Objects:** Group similar objects together to minimize unnecessary collision checks. For example, group all vehicles together and all pedestrians together.

### Step 2: Implement Spatial Partitioning

#### 2.1. **Choose a Spatial Partitioning Method**
   - **Grid-Based Partitioning:** Divide the simulation space into a grid where each cell contains objects that are close to each other.
   - **Quadtree/Octree Partitioning:** Use a hierarchical structure to divide the space into smaller regions. This is particularly useful for dynamic environments.

#### 2.2. **Implement Grid-Based Partitioning**
   - **Create a Grid Structure:**
     ```cpp
     struct GridCell {
         std::vector<PxActor*> actors;
     };

     std::vector<GridCell> gridCells;
     int gridSize = 10; // Number of cells per dimension
     float cellSize = 10.0f; // Size of each cell

     void initializeGrid() {
         gridCells.resize(gridSize * gridSize);
         for (int i = 0; i < gridSize * gridSize; ++i) {
             gridCells[i].actors.clear();
         }
     }

     void updateGrid(PxActor* actor, PxVec3 position) {
         int x = static_cast<int>(position.x / cellSize);
         int y = static_cast<int>(position.y / cellSize);

         if (x >= 0 && x < gridSize && y >= 0 && y < gridSize) {
             int index = y * gridSize + x;
             gridCells[index].actors.push_back(actor);
         }
     }
     ```

   - **Perform Collision Checks Within Cells:**
     ```cpp
     void checkCollisions() {
         for (auto& cell : gridCells) {
             for (size_t i = 0; i < cell.actors.size(); ++i) {
                 for (size_t j = i + 1; j < cell.actors.size(); ++j) {
                     PxActor* actorA = cell.actors[i];
                     PxActor* actorB = cell.actors[j];

                     // Perform collision check between actorA and actorB
                     // Example: PxPairFlags flags = PxPairFlag::eCONTACT_DEFAULT;
                     //          PxContactPairHeader header;
                     //          PxContactPair* pairs;
                     //          PxU32 count = PxGetNumContacts(actorA, actorB);
                     //          PxGetContacts(actorA, actorB, header, pairs, count);
                 }
             }
         }
     }
     ```

#### 2.3. **Implement Quadtree/Octree Partitioning**
   - **Define the Tree Structure:**
     ```cpp
     struct OctreeNode {
         std::vector<PxActor*> actors;
         std::array<std::unique_ptr<OctreeNode>, 8> children;
         PxBounds3 bounds;
     };

     std::unique_ptr<OctreeNode> root;

     void initializeTree(const PxBounds3& worldBounds) {
         root = std::make_unique<OctreeNode>();
         root->bounds = worldBounds;
         root->actors.clear();
     }

     void insertActor(OctreeNode* node, PxActor* actor, const PxBounds3& actorBounds) {
         if (node->children[0] == nullptr) {
             // Subdivide the node if it doesn't have children yet
             PxBounds3 childBounds = node->bounds;
             float halfSize = childBounds.getExtents().x / 2.0f;
             for (int i = 0; i < 8; ++i) {
                 node->children[i] = std::make_unique<OctreeNode>();
                 node->children[i]->bounds = childBounds;
                 node->children[i]->bounds.minimum += PxVec3((i & 1) ? halfSize : -halfSize,
                                                             (i & 2) ? halfSize : -halfSize,
                                                             (i & 4) ? halfSize : -halfSize);
             }
         }

         // Find the correct child node for the actor
         int childIndex = 0;
         if (actorBounds.minimum.x > node->bounds.minimum.x + halfSize) childIndex |= 1;
         if (actorBounds.minimum.y > node->bounds.minimum.y + halfSize) childIndex |= 2;
         if (actorBounds.minimum.z > node->bounds.minimum.z + halfSize) childIndex |= 4;

         if (node->children[childIndex]->bounds.contains(actorBounds)) {
             insertActor(node->children[childIndex].get(), actor, actorBounds);
         } else {
             node->actors.push_back(actor);
         }
     }
     ```

   - **Perform Collision Checks Within Nodes:**
     ```cpp
