### Step 3: Interpret AddressSanitizer Output

AddressSanitizer will print a summary of memory leaks at the end of your program's execution. It will show the number of leaks and provide stack traces for each leak.

For example, the output might look something like this:

```
==12345==ERROR: LeakSanitizer: detected memory leaks

Direct leak of 4000000 byte(s) in 1 object(s) allocated from:
    #0 0x4c4c4c4c in operator new[](unsigned long) (/path/to/libasan.so+0x4c4c4c4c)
    #1 0x4c4c4c4c in SensorData::SensorData() (/path/to/my_simulation+0x4c4c4c4c)
