### 1. Use Multi-Threading
PhysX supports multi-threading, which can help distribute the workload across multiple CPU cores.

### 2. Simplify Physics Models
Simplify the physics models used for less critical actors. For example, use simpler shapes or fewer constraints for distant or less interactive objects.

### 3. Use Level of Detail (LOD)
Implement level of detail (LOD) for physics models. Use simpler models for distant objects and more detailed models for closer objects.

### 4. Disable Unnecessary Features
Disable features that are not necessary for your simulation, such as continuous collision detection (CCD) or advanced constraint solving, to reduce computational overhead.

### 5. Optimize Collision Detection
Optimize collision detection by using broad-phase algorithms and spatial partitioning techniques.

### 6. Use Fixed Timestep
Use a fixed timestep for physics simulation to ensure consistent performance.

