    return np.all(relative_error <= tolerance)
```

### Step 3: Use Fixtures in Test Cases

Use the fixtures in your test cases to ensure smooth setup and comparison.

```python
import pytest
import numpy as np

# Existing fixtures
@pytest.fixture
def baseline_data():
    return np.array([1, 2, 3])

@pytest.fixture
def optimized_data():
    return np.array([1.001, 2.001, 3.001])

# Function to compare results
def compare_results(baseline, optimized, tolerance=0.001):
    relative_error = np.abs((baseline - optimized) / baseline)
    return np.all(relative_error <= tolerance)

# Regression test function
def test_physics_optimization(baseline_data, optimized_data):
